---
import SectionLabel from "../../elements/SectionLabel.astro";
import Heading from "../../elements/Heading.astro";
import BodyText from "../../elements/BodyText.astro";
---

<section class="py-16 md:py-24">
  <div class="container-default">
    <figure
      class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-[14px] border border-us-brass/50"
      data-reveal
    >
      <img
        src="/assets/img/people/clark-on-stage.jpg"
        alt="Clark Sell on stage at THAT Conference in front of a slide that reads: What has heart and meaning for you?"
        width="799"
        height="533"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
        class="block w-full h-auto aspect-3/2 object-cover"
      />
      <figcaption
        class="absolute bottom-0 inset-x-0 px-5 py-4 bg-linear-to-t from-us-ink/80 to-transparent font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-us-paper/90"
      >
        Clark on stage at THAT Conference
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div
      class="mt-20 md:mt-28 grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16"
    >
      <div class="lg:col-span-4">
        <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-32" data-reveal>
          <SectionLabel number="01" text="The name" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-8">
        <Heading size="md" class="max-w-[22ch]" data-reveal>
          “Unspecified” is what you call a thing before anyone decides what it's
          for.
        </Heading>
        <BodyText class="mt-8 max-w-[58ch]" data-reveal>
          We kept the name because it turned out to be honest. We've never been
          defined by one product, one platform, or one stack. We've shipped
          software used by millions of people and built communities that outgrew
          us. Today, all of it points at one thing: Troth.
        </BodyText>
        <BodyText class="mt-5 max-w-[58ch]" data-reveal>
          What has never been unspecified is the reason. From the beginning, our
          mission has been to create software that connects people in a deeper,
          more meaningful way. It's still the test every project has to pass.
        </BodyText>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div
      class="mt-20 md:mt-28 grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-16"
    >
      <div class="lg:col-span-4">
        <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-32" data-reveal>
          <SectionLabel number="02" text="How we work" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-8">
        <Heading size="md" class="max-w-[22ch]" data-reveal>
          Founder-owned. Founder-run. Nobody between you and the people who made
          the thing.
        </Heading>
        <BodyText class="mt-8 max-w-[58ch]" data-reveal>
          We write our own code. We answer our own email. We ship what we would
          want to use ourselves, and we build it with the people who are going
          to use it. When you write to Unspecified, one of us reads it.
        </BodyText>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
